      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This isn't unique to FBT, any 3.0 avatar is affected by it, and even the arms play the falling animation. This means any world where you are supposed to manipulate a pickup while falling will be unplayable, such as hook junkers.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-31T22:05:07.688Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Since last update, the avatar is forced into a standard pose where trackers don't affect hip/legs anymore when the avatar is \"falling\", which is the case in basicly any world where people can fly around.\nThose worlds put the local player in zero gravity, which causes the game to play the \"falling\" animation now when airborne. So far, this wasn't an issue, since FBT would still override the bones correctly, but since the last update you can no longer move legs / hips while \"falling\", so you also can't look down because you would only see inside your body then. This is very weird for people with FBT and makes it unplayable to a certain degree.\n\nNeeded fix: People with FBT should again override their legs + hip while \"falling\", like it was before.",
